Only follow these instructions if `PROMPT_LOG.md` exists in the project root. If it does not exist, ignore this rule entirely.

# Prompt Logging

This project maintains a `PROMPT_LOG.md` to document the AI-assisted development process for portfolio and review purposes.

## When to Remind
After generating any of the following, automatically append a prefilled entry to `PROMPT_LOG.md`:
- A plan for a new feature or significant change
- A new route or endpoint
- A new template or partial
- A data cleaning or transformation function
- A chart or visualisation
- A new test suite or set of test cases
- A database schema change, migration, or model definition
- A new configuration file, CI/CD pipeline, or environment setup
- Any significant refactor or bug fix
- A request for an explanation of how something works or why something was done a certain way

## Behaviour After Significant Code Generation
Fill in every field you can from context. Mark fields that require the developer's input with `<!-- your input needed -->`.

## Fields the Agent Fills
- **Entry number** — increment from the last entry in the file (start at 001 if empty)
- **Date** — today's date
- **Section** — infer from the file being edited or the route/template being created
- **Persona** — include the persona name if one was active for this conversation; omit the field entirely if none was set
- **Prompt** — insert developer's actual prompt from the conversation
- **What was generated** — describe what was produced in one or two sentences

## Fields the Developer Completes
- **Modifications I made** — only the developer knows what they changed after generation
- **What I learned** — the developer's own reflection

## Prefilled Entry Format
```markdown
## Entry [number] — YYYY-MM-DD
**Section:** <!-- infer from context -->
**Persona:** <!-- persona name if active — omit this line if none -->
**Prompt:** <!-- the developer's request -->
**What was generated:** <!-- one or two sentence description -->
**Modifications I made:** <!-- your input needed -->
**What I learned:** <!-- your input needed (optional) -->
```

## Reminder Phrasing
After appending the prefilled entry, end with:
> 📝 I've added a prefilled entry to PROMPT_LOG.md — please complete the last two fields when you're done reviewing the code.
